    <node id="Registry Entry">
      <data key="d0">Registry Entry</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">**Registry Entry**

A Registry Entry is a formal record maintained within the fictional reference world’s registry system. It serves as a generic yet comprehensive repository for relational data, documenting assertions, relationships, and information about other entries or subregions. Each entry captures a stated relationship between two identifiers, providing a structured description of how those entities are connected. The record may include source assertions indicating the provenance of the information, and it can encompass details about subregions and their specific relationships. In particular, a Registry Entry records the relationship between two subregions and may also record a source assertion about the relationship between a subregion and its parent region. Overall, the entry functions as a record that describes the relationship between two identifiers while documenting any associated source assertions and additional information about the involved entities.&lt;SEP&gt;An abstract representation of a record in a registry system.</data>
      <data key="d3">D012c0031b1c2d5f5b85e-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;D05bcb6c31f6fea61f984-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;D112f091f348d72661fce-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;D1759848a15f03afde86d-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;D25fbde5780c9df0a16a1-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;D307f61e2bb61c65dbffa-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;D32fee42740fc2d3298a6-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;D3bf755801edbd55b30c7-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;D3ef4f03e9b791e37b6ba-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;D47c49cfab181f97b6a71-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;D69ab7fa586361d0bba4c-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;D6ae5922c2a4aebab2026-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;D6af3230e4a34d9d96ade-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;D6bc36a09c6ec8f5132fb-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;D76413fefe6657c0277f5-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;D79e87d2f4d1f958bca1f-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;D813a5727276cc4bd97d1-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;D87e6c533b79da8158b89-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;D92b87fb4dd790a9a0f2f-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;D9c01ceca580f57a3a888-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;D9ef8a07e4e94f4e5961c-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;D9f759ab27061c634112b-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;Db4656d39a9d08594c964-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;Db4dcda9f1198705b8e51-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;Db8ef2d8f24e3cb70b9e7-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;Dbb866ffea43863d04da8-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;Dc3ec77827ceea4dcff0a-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;Dc9320332e07435936dd6-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;Dd1b71a1b0a096adfd662-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;De3f35bb5cd2daf23678e-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;De5d52bc41134b6f51dcf-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;De791e97b2b1adf07df4f-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;Deb75e238ae54da5ebf3e-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;Decaa8fc6b15beb60ce58-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;Decdf71c98e5febd35406-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;Df08f83e6fbc691cf3e31-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;Dfa1b226b2a08def00dc8-chunk-000</data>
